  "notes": "Cash-basis county, governmental funds only. Statement lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5): fund balance 8,518,792 + receipts 7,097,674 - disbursements 6,302,975 + transfers in 1,504,664 - transfers out 1,504,664 = 9,313,491. Ending cash = Cash and Cash Equivalents 9,313,491 (p3, equal to the Statement of Net Position p1); no prior-year cash printed, so beginning_cash null. Taxes 3,400,090 has no printed type breakdown (Statement of Activities p2 prints one Taxes line); split only by fund name: Inheritance Tax Fund 565,193 (inheritance tax), Visitor Promotion 3,725 and Visitor Improvement 1,863 (lodging tax); remainder 2,829,309 (General 2,724,511 + Hospital Bond 82,651 + 911 Emergency 22,147) stays taxes. Intergovernmental kept as one line (includes ARPA 485,887). Balance sheet: governmental funds Statement of Cash Basis Assets and Fund Balances (p3-4) Total column, equal to the Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p7); major (p8-9) and nonmajor (p10-15) fund budget schedules, one per fund; funds with only zero actuals (Emergency Bridge, Drug Law Enforcement, LEC Block Grant, Wireless E911 Service, Juvenile Diversion) have no lines; the nonmajor combining statement (p17, first page only in the trim) duplicates the budget schedules and is not recorded. Disbursement functions for the one-line fund schedules come from the statement fund columns (p5-6, p17); Records Preservation / Equipment Sinking (general government) and Highway Buyback / Noxious Weed (public works) derived from the nonmajor function totals. General Fund other financing total -200,078 is printed on the statement (p5) only. The 911 Emergency Fund schedule (p11) prints a taxes variance (578) where budget 23,819 - actual 22,147 = 1,672 (variance column only; not recorded). Read pages 1-17 of 17"
